{"ini_file":"CTHConstants.ini","provenance":"build_ini_schemas.py 2026-06-07 | data=C:\\Jagged Alliance 2\\Jagged Alliance 2 Gold 1.13 Mod Prototype - Copy\\Data-1.13 | engine=C:\\AI Projects\\The Wasteland\\Visual Studio Root","sections":[{"name":"General","description":"","properties":[{"name":"NORMAL_SHOOTING_DISTANCE","datatype":"numeric","default":"70","min":"10","max":"10000","vanilla":null,"description":"This setting represents the longest distance at which Iron Sights are 100% effective.\nBeyond this range, shooting accuracy begins to drop, and a scope will be required\nto avoid that drop.\nALL SCOPE RANGES ARE DETERMINED BY THIS VALUE. For instance, a 2x scope will\nnegate penalties for shooting at twice this distance. A 10x scope will\nnegate penalties for shooting at ten times this distance.\nBy decreasing this value, you can make all shots more accurate, and naturally\nmake scopes more powerful.\nThis value is an INTEGER, with a range of 10 to 1000. The distance is\nmeasured in METERS, not tiles, so 100 means 10 tiles.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"70","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3673","default":"70","min":"10","max":"10000"}},{"name":"IRON_SIGHT_PERFORMANCE_BONUS","datatype":"numeric","default":"20.0","min":"-50.0","max":"50.0","vanilla":null,"description":"------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe following parameters in this block are used only if USE_NEW_CTH_CALCULATION = TRUE in your Ja2_Options.ini\nBe aware that IRON_SIGHT_PERFORMANCE_BONUS and LASER_PERFORMANCE_BONUS_IRON are cumulative!\n\nIRON_SIGHT_PERFORMANCE_BONUS affects the size of the base shooting aperture for iron sights by x percent.\nValues can go from -50.0 (penalty) to 50.0 (bonus of 50 percent will make the aperture half as large)\nThe default is 20.0","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"20.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3674","default":"0.0","min":"-50.0","max":"50.0"}},{"name":"LASER_PERFORMANCE_BONUS_HIP","datatype":"numeric","default":"25.0","min":"0.0","max":"50.0","vanilla":null,"description":"LASER_PERFORMANCE_BONUS_XXX also affects the size of the base shooting aperture by x percent but is used for lasers.\nThe bonus only applies if the target is in laser range and the given sight is used.\nThe bonus is also influenced by the light level at the target spot. The darker the spot the better the laser dot\ncan be seen and the higher the resulting bonus will be.\nIf all values are 0.0 the old NCTH laser behaviour is used which makes lasers work like scopes.\nValues can go from 0.0 to 50.0","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"25.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3675","default":"0.0","min":"0.0","max":"50.0"}},{"name":"LASER_PERFORMANCE_BONUS_IRON","datatype":"numeric","default":"15.0","min":"0.0","max":"50.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"15.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3676","default":"0.0","min":"0.0","max":"50.0"}},{"name":"LASER_PERFORMANCE_BONUS_SCOPE","datatype":"numeric","default":"10.0","min":"0.0","max":"50.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"10.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3677","default":"0.0","min":"0.0","max":"50.0"}},{"name":"DEGREES_MAXIMUM_APERTURE","datatype":"numeric","default":"15","min":"0.0","max":"22.5","vanilla":null,"description":"This is the maximum angle, to either side of the shooter, that a bullet may fly.\nThe CTH system works by shooting bullets randomly inside this angle. Increasing\nyour aim will make the angle smaller, thus making rounds more likely to hit the\ntarget.\n\nThis value is a FLOAT, with a range of 0 to 22.5. If set to 0, all shots will\nbe 100% on target, regardless of aiming.\nDecreasing this value causes all shots to be more accurate.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"15","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3678","default":"15.0","min":"0.0","max":"22.5"}},{"name":"IRON_SIGHTS_MAX_APERTURE_USE_GRADIENT","datatype":"boolean","default":"TRUE","min":null,"max":null,"vanilla":null,"description":"This option affects DEGREES_MAXIMUM_APERTURE for iron sights. If it is set to FALSE\nthe basic aperture will grow linearly to the distance to target (old behaviour).\nIf TRUE the aperture will use a curve to grow slower over distance making iron sights\nmore powerful over long distances.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"TRUE","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3679","default":"FALSE"}},{"name":"IRON_SIGHTS_MAX_APERTURE_MODIFIER","datatype":"numeric","default":"3.0","min":"2.0","max":"5.0","vanilla":null,"description":"If IRON_SIGHTS_MAX_APERTURE_USE_GRADIENT is TRUE the following parameter defines\nhow fast the aperture will grow. A lower value will make it grow slower thus making\niron sights even more powerful.\nA value of 2.0 will make iron sights almost as powerful as a 2x scope whereas a value\nof 5.0 causes just a little change from the old behaviour.\nValues can go from 2.0 to 5.0\nThe default is 3.0","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"3.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3680","default":"3.0","min":"2.0","max":"5.0"}},{"name":"RANGE_COEFFICIENT","datatype":"numeric","default":"1.1","min":"0.001","max":"100.0","vanilla":null,"description":"The Range Coefficient works with the listed weapon range to determine the weapons\nmaximum range.  Once a bullet reaches it's maximum range, gravity pulls it towards\nthe ground.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"1.1","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3681","default":"2.0","min":"0.001","max":"100.0"}},{"name":"GRAVITY_COEFFICIENT","datatype":"numeric","default":"6.0","min":"0.001","max":"100.0","vanilla":null,"description":"The Gravity Coefficient determines how powerful gravity is once it kicks into\naction - this happens when the bullet reaches the \"maximum range\" of the gun\nthat fired it.\nThe lower this coefficient, the faster will bullets change their trajectory\ntowards the ground, hitting it sooner.\nConversely, by increasing this value you can let bullets fly further beyond\nthe max range of the gun. That will effectively let guns hit targets further\nbeyond their max range, though it is not a reliable way to hit any target.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"6.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3682","default":"1.0","min":"0.001","max":"100.0"}},{"name":"VERTICAL_BIAS","datatype":"numeric","default":"0.5","min":"0.01","max":"2.0","vanilla":null,"description":"The Vertical Bias \"flattens\" the target aperture which restricts the vertical amount\nby which a bullet can travel.  Vertical bias is ultimately based on stance where\na standing shooter is always at 1.0, a prone shooter is at the indicated bias, and\na crouching target is midway between the two.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"0.5","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3683","default":"1.0","min":"0.01","max":"2.0"}},{"name":"SCOPE_RANGE_MULTIPLIER","datatype":"numeric","default":"0.7","min":"0.1","max":"1.5","vanilla":null,"description":"The Scope Range Multiplier is applied against a scopes magnification to determine\nthe scopes minimum effective range.  Sniper and Hunter training has a slight effect\non this.  Valid range is 0.5 - 1.5, with a default of 0.7.  The higher you set\nthis multiplier, the less effective scopes become.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"0.7","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3684","default":"0.7","min":"0.1","max":"1.5"}},{"name":"SCOPE_EFFECTIVENESS_MULTIPLIER","datatype":"numeric","default":"1.1","min":"0.5","max":"1.5","vanilla":null,"description":"Scope effectiveness multiplier defines the upper limit of the scopes magnification\nthat is achievable by any shooter. Scope magnification makes the size of the\nshooting aperture smaller, making shots more accurate. A multiplier of 1.0 will\nmake a 2x scope provide a maximum of 2x magnification (make the aiming reticule\nhalf as large). A low skill shooter will only be able to achieve a much smaller\neffective magnification. Scope effectiveness is determined by a shooters experience\nand marksmanship attributes. Attributes are weighted by AIM_EXP and AIM_MARKS.\nValid values are from 0.5 to 1.5 with a default of 1.1","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"1.1","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3690","default":"1.1","min":"0.5","max":"1.5"}},{"name":"SCOPE_EFFECTIVENESS_MINIMUM","datatype":"numeric","default":"50","min":"0","max":"100","vanilla":null,"description":"Scope effectiveness minimum defines a minimum percentage of scope effectiveness\nthat any merc will achieve no matter how bad/good his skills are (see also description\nof SCOPE_EFFECTIVENESS_MULTIPLIER above) For example if the parameter is 50 a 2x scope\nwill provide at least 1x magnification. The rest comes from the shooters experience\nand marksmanship. A value of 0 will make effectiveness calculation fully dynamic.\n100 means that the shooters skills are irrelevant and he can use any scope to its\nfull potential.\nValid values are from 0 to 100 with a default of 50","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"50","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3691","default":"50","min":"0","max":"100"}},{"name":"SCOPE_EFFECTIVENESS_MINIMUM_RANGER","datatype":"numeric","default":"80","min":"0","max":"100","vanilla":null,"description":"Certain traits provide their own fixed minimum values. Defaults are 80 / 90 / 100\nIf the shooter wants to exceed these he will have to do so by the normal formula.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"80","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3692","default":"80","min":"0","max":"100"}},{"name":"SCOPE_EFFECTIVENESS_MINIMUM_MARKSMAN","datatype":"numeric","default":"90","min":"0","max":"100","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"90","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3693","default":"90","min":"0","max":"100"}},{"name":"SCOPE_EFFECTIVENESS_MINIMUM_SNIPER","datatype":"numeric","default":"100","min":"0","max":"100","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"100","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3694","default":"100","min":"0","max":"100"}},{"name":"SIDE_FACING_DIVISOR","datatype":"numeric","default":"1.0","min":"1.0","max":"10.0","vanilla":null,"description":"The Side Facing Divisor is applied against the shooting offsets when a target is\nfacing directly perpendicular (i.e., East or West when shooter faces North or South)\nto the shooter.  This is to account for a visual error in the NCTH system.  The\nValid range for this divisor is 1.0 - 10.0.  If you don't think it should be as easy\nto hit a target from the side as from head on, just set this value to 1.0","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"1.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3695","default":"2.0","min":"1.0","max":"10.0"}},{"name":"BASIC_RELIABILITY_ODDS","datatype":"numeric","default":"45","min":"0","max":"10000","vanilla":null,"description":"This is the basic chance PER SHOT to lose 1 point of weapon condition with each\nbullet fired. The formula for this chance is 1 in BASE_DEPRECIATE_CHANCE, so higher\nvalues result in slower degradation.\nThe default value for OCTH is 15, but NCTH requires a **much** higher\nexpenditure of bullets, resulting in severely-reduced weapon condition after every\nbattle. Therefore, the default for NCTH is currently 150.\nValid range is 0-10000.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"45","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3697","default":"15","min":"0","max":"10000"}}]},{"name":"Base CTH","description":"","properties":[{"name":"BASE_EXP","datatype":"numeric","default":"3.0","min":"0.0","max":"100.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"3.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3703","default":"3.0","min":"0.0","max":"100.0"}},{"name":"BASE_MARKS","datatype":"numeric","default":"1.0","min":"0.0","max":"100.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"1.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3704","default":"1.0","min":"0.0","max":"100.0"}},{"name":"BASE_WIS","datatype":"numeric","default":"1.0","min":"0.0","max":"100.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"1.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3705","default":"1.0","min":"0.0","max":"100.0"}},{"name":"BASE_DEX","datatype":"numeric","default":"1.0","min":"0.0","max":"100.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"1.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3706","default":"1.0","min":"0.0","max":"100.0"}},{"name":"BASE_LOW_MORALE","datatype":"numeric","default":"-1.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This is a modifier given per each morale point below 50.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-1.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3708","default":"-1.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_HIGH_MORALE","datatype":"numeric","default":"2.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This modifier is given per each morale point above 50.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"2.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3709","default":"2.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_PSYCHO","datatype":"numeric","default":"-3.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This modifier is given to any character with the \"PSYCHO\" trait.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-3.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3710","default":"-3.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_SHOOTING_UPWARDS","datatype":"numeric","default":"-15.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This is the modifier given when shooting one \"cube\" upwards. A cube is\n1/3 of a tile high. This takes into account both stance and level. For\nexample, a standing merc shooting at the legs of a target on the roof\ngets 1*this modifier. A prone merc on ground level shooting at the\nhead of a target on ground level gets 2*this modifier.\n\nThe shooting upwards modifier is then divided by the range to the target\n(in tiles). In other words, at a range of 2 tiles the modifier is\nHALVED. at a range of 10 tiles, the modifier is divided by 10. Etcetera.\nThis means that the further the target is, the less relevant the upwards\nangle is.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-15.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3711","default":"-15.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_INJURY","datatype":"numeric","default":"-30.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This is the MAXIMUM modifier given to a shooter when injured. To get this\nmuch, the shooter must be dead (0% health...). It's linear,\nso at 50% health the shooter gets exactly half the penalty.\nNote that \"Bandaged\" damage counts as half as much as bleeding damage.\nTherefore, 50% bandaged damage is as bad as only25% bleeding damage.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-30.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3712","default":"-30.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_DRUNK_TIPSY","datatype":"numeric","default":"-5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-5.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3713","default":"-5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_DRUNK","datatype":"numeric","default":"-20.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-20.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3714","default":"-20.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_DRUNK_WASTED","datatype":"numeric","default":"-50.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-50.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3715","default":"-50.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_DRUNK_HUNGOVER","datatype":"numeric","default":"-10.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-10.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3716","default":"-10.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_FATIGUE","datatype":"numeric","default":"-15.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This is the MAXIMUM modifier given to a shooter when fully fatigued (0% breath).\nIt's linear, so at 50% breath you get half the modifier.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-15.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3717","default":"-15.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_SAME_TARGET","datatype":"numeric","default":"5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This modifier is applied when shooting at the same target again. If the target\nhas moved between shots, or the shooter does anything but shoot at the target,\nthe modifier is lost.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"5.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3718","default":"5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_GASSED","datatype":"numeric","default":"-15.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This is the modifier given when the shooter is in a cloud of gas and does\nnot have a gas mask on.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-15.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3719","default":"-15.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_BEING_BANDAGED","datatype":"numeric","default":"-5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This modifier is applied when the shooter is being bandaged by someone else.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-5.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3720","default":"-5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_SHOCK","datatype":"numeric","default":"-150.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This is the MAXIMUM modifier given when the target reaches the maximum number\nof Suppression Shock points, which by default would be 30. It's linear, so at\n15 shock points you get half the penalty.\nNote that characters with high experience stop accumulating shock much earlier,\nand so are much less subject to this modifier than other characters.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-150.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3721","default":"-150.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_AGILE_TARGET","datatype":"numeric","default":"-5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This modifier is applied if the target has exceptional agility or experience level.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-5.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3722","default":"-5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_TARGET_INVISIBLE","datatype":"numeric","default":"-100.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"This modifier is applied if the shooter can't see the target. This happens\nwhen shooting at a target spotted by someone else.","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"-100.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3723","default":"-100.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_DRAW_COST","datatype":"numeric","default":"2.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"2.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3725","default":"2.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_TWO_GUNS","datatype":"numeric","default":"5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"5.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3726","default":"5.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_ONE_HANDED","datatype":"numeric","default":"2.5","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"2.5","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3727","default":"2.5","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_STANDING_STANCE","datatype":"numeric","default":"2.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"2.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3728","default":"2.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_CROUCHING_STANCE","datatype":"numeric","default":"3.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"3.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3729","default":"3.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0"}},{"name":"BASE_PRONE_STANCE","datatype":"numeric","default":"4.0","min":"-1000.0","max":"1000.0","vanilla":null,"description":"","list_values":[],"confidence":"engine","interval":null,"shipped":"4.0","engine":{"loader":"Ja2/GameSettings.cpp:3730","default":"4.0","min":"-1000